2026-09-13T02:47:10.0606880Z [36;1m## -- Detect an unreleased R --[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0607277Z [36;1m# The persistent ccache below is keyed on getRversion(), and that key is[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0607863Z [36;1m# only honest for a released R, where the version number changes[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0608367Z [36;1m# whenever the installation does. R-devel is rebuilt every day but keeps[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0608874Z [36;1m# reporting the same number for months, so one cache entry ends up[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0609360Z [36;1m# serving an arbitrary span of R-devel snapshots -- and restoring it in[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0609849Z [36;1m# the rcc R-devel job has produced build failures. Skip the persistent[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0610326Z [36;1m# cache there and build cold; ccache itself stays configured by the[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0611507Z [36;1m# install action, so reuse within the job is unaffected.[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0611997Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0612308Z [36;1m# R.version$status is empty for a released R and non-empty for one that[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0612804Z [36;1m# moves under a fixed version number ("Under development (unstable)" for[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0613298Z [36;1m# R-devel, "Patched" for R-patched) -- exactly the builds the key cannot[0m
2026-09-13T02:47:10.0613659Z [36;1m# tell apart.[0m
